// no target needs new instruction selection: `width` is 1, 2 or 4.
// C arrays inline in extern records (`f: [T; N]`) are copied whole into and out of Grail vectors.
// kind 0: integers and words (`size` bytes, sign-extended when `signed`); 1: f32 (binary32 in
// memory, binary64 in Grail); 2: extern records of `size` bytes, each a fresh `words`-word record;
// 3: bytes, into and out of a Grail byte sequence (`[u8; N]`); 4: 32-bit units into and out of a
// narrow vector (`f32[]`, `u32[]`, `i32[]` store binary32 bits and low words already, as C does).
fn rt_carray_load(src: u64, n: u64, size: u64, signed: u64, kind: u64, words: u64) -> u64 {
