// ---- flat vectors: elements of `w` bytes stored inline (docs/design/unboxed-values.md, 1b) ----
// A vector of plain records or `extern "C"` records holds the elements' bytes, `w` each, after one
// another; the header is the same {pointer, length, capacity}, counted in elements. A value taken out
// of one is a box of its own (rt_flat_box); a value put in is copied from its box, which is freed.
fn rt_flat_box(src: u64, w: u64) -> u64 {
    // Rounded up to whole words; rt_div is a software division and this runs per element.
    box := rt_alloc((w + 7) & 18446744073709551608);
    rt_copy_bytes(box, src, w);
    return box;
